      "iso_date": "2026-09-13T03:50:04Z",
      "iso_date_of_last_edit": "2026-09-14T12:06:19Z",
      "text": "We went to this Samara Veg especially for breakfast at the Chikkaballapur branch. We had previously visited their other outlet, around 40 km further ahead, and had an amazing experience, so we decided to drive from Bengaluru to try this one as well. Thankfully, this branch did not disappoint either!\n\nI really appreciated the thoughtful little touches here — mint lemon water, a wheelchair ramp, a mini washbasin for kids in the washroom, and a kids’ play area. These may seem like small things, but they make the place feel much more welcoming and family-friendly.\n\nThe food was tasty and lived up to our expectations. We ordered Pongal, masala dosa, rava idli, kesari bath, tea, and jaggery coffee. The Pongal was different from what is usually served at their other outlet, but in a refreshing and delicious way. The masala dosa was slightly cold, but still tasty. Rava idli was good, and the kesari bath was absolutely delicious. The tea was a little too sweet for my liking, but otherwise tasted good.\n\nThe jaggery coffee was a nice addition. It had a good coffee flavour without being overly sweet, so the sweetness didn’t overpower the coffee.\n\nThe washrooms were clean, and the overall place was hygienic, well-maintained, and thoughtfully designed. The only area that could be improved is the service speed. Placing the order and sometimes having to repeat it can get a little frustrating. However, once the order is placed correctly, the food is served quite quickly.\n\nOverall, it was definitely worth the drive from Bengaluru. A nice place for a family breakfast, with good food, clean surroundings, and some thoughtful touches that make the experience better. Would happily visit again!\n\nIf you want, I can also make this **shorter and more punchy for a Google review**, while keeping the same points.",
